Perhaps, but remember, you had virtually every item essential to winning
the game plus an intrinsic -38 AC.  If you've ever played a game where 
you can't find seven candles, you'll see how 'easy' the game is then!  
Essentially, high level characters are meant to be powerful--after all,
it's not as if some wimp 10th level 3 int barbarian can be a demigod(dess).
So I have no problem with the relative power of high level characters.
As well, you probably knew a lot about the endgame and the subtle methods
of death that usually kill off high-level chars--think of the poor novice
who finally has a good game, only to be killed in the elemental planes
due to ignorance.  Want to make the game nearly impossible to win without
reading rec.games.hack?  I don't.

>Finally, the bell of opening needs to be changed --- either
