A large part of the power of high level characters is due to a cursed
Bell of Opening.  Having a lot of levels helps you to hit monsters, to
make your saving throw against petrification, and so forth.  The extra
hit points don't hurt either!  This is the one aspect of the game that
needs work.  Some demigod around here ascended with 962 hit points.

>Having a rock mole eat the bell is a rather ridiculous way to be 
>permanently screwed. 

This is why you can wish for artifacts. :)

It seems that Mr. Lodenkamper wishes to make the level of difficulty
more even throughout the game, but I must (respectfully) disagree, seeing
as I've had three potential demigods go awry because of some silly reason
or another.  Once your character is past a certain point, he deserves to
win unless you spaz horribly.  If the level of difficulty is the same
throughout, it seems random chance will dictate whether a given character
will ascend or not. 
